<div class="text-left">
    <h5>Explanation of how injectors work</h5>
    <ul>
        <li>0 to 50 million talent points at time of purchase = 100% of talent points injected</li>
        <li>50 to 100 million talent points at time of purchase = 80% of talent points injected</li>
        <li>100 to 150 million talent points at time of purchase = 60% of talent points injected</li>
        <li>150 to 250 million talent points at time of purchase = 40% of talent points injected</li>
        <li>250 million or more talent points at time of purchase = 20% of talent points injected</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
        Overall talent points are the sum of allocated and unallocated talent points. So, if a character has 49,501,000 talent points before injection and two talent injectors (500,000) are used, the amount of talent points he will receive are 900,000. The first talent injector will add 500,000 TP, but as it brings the total amount of talent points to 50,001,000, the character is over the limit and only receives 400,000 TP from the second injector accordingly.
    </p>
</div>